cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this analysis code, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "Procedural outcomes of image-guided central venous access port placement across the body mass index spectrum: a post hoc analysis of a prospective multicenter registry"
authors:
  - family-names: "MITSUHASHI"
    given-names: "TOSHIHARU"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9940-0570"
    affiliation: "Center for Innovative Clinical Medicine, Medical Development Field, Okayama University"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  Stata analysis code for a post hoc analysis of a prospective multicenter
  registry examining the association between BMI and procedural outcomes of
  image-guided central venous access port placement. The code includes
  descriptive statistics, modified Poisson regression, linear regression,
  and restricted cubic spline analyses. Patient-level data are not included.
keywords:
  - "Stata"
  - "body mass index"
  - "central venous access port"
  - "image-guided port placement"
  - "restricted cubic splines"
